  message: "CLOSED done — PR #148, dev 2d6dc7803d (2026-08-01).\n\nAll three filed failure modes fixed, each pinned by a behavioral test\ndriving the REAL script (tests/test_autopr_vpr_reconcile.py):\n\n1. Non-ff rejection classified: remote-tip-equals-local -> proceed as\n   pushed; diverged -> loud NOT-queueing error (rc 2), handled at both\n   the do_pr and flush call sites. The observed phantom-vPR mint (the\n   PR #144 duplicate) is structurally impossible on this path now.\n2. prune judges CONTENT identity with .ci/affected-tests.txt excluded:\n   tree-identity vs base tip + bounded filtered-patch-id scan (100\n   commits). The measured manifest-noise-only entry now prunes; a\n   genuinely-unmerged entry stays; an EMPTY commit is exempt from\n   content judgment (ancestry only) — a refinement the pre-existing\n   allow-empty fixtures caught during the sweep.\n3. Unresolvable-sha entries are a third BROKEN reconciliation class:\n   prune drops them with an explicit unverifiable-content warning;\n   flush pre-diagnoses and points at prune instead of dying on git raw\n   \"Needed a single revision\".\n\n92/92 across the seven auto-pr suites. Closure evidence includes the\nmeta-proof: PR #148 was itself pushed and merged by the fixed script."  # 3bc5
